NAME
    more - page through text a screenful at a time

SYNOPSIS
    more [file]

DESCRIPTION
    Displays a file (or standard input) one page at a time. After each
    page it prints "--More--" and waits for a console key. The paging key
    is always read from the console, so more still works at the end of a
    pipe. more is a /bin program.

    Keys at the --More-- prompt:
        space   next full page
        Enter   one more line
        q, Q    quit
        other   next full page

EXAMPLES
    more BIG.TXT
    dir -R | more

SEE ALSO
    cat, head, tail
